## MUST-FIX 1 — P157 invariant dropped its scope condition (SCOPE_BROADENED, non-negotiable tier)

Root cause: `compile_invariants._to_invariant` reduces a principle to its **first sentence**;
P157's bound ("in a system-paced presentation") lived in the second sentence, so the adapter
carried the narration-over-onscreen-text prescription unconditioned at its highest-precedence tier
while `profile.yaml` and `skills/multimedia-and-elearning-design/SKILL.md` both kept the bound.

Fix (root, not adapter): reordered P157's `statement` in `principles/principles.yaml` so the first
sentence is self-sufficient. Same two clauses, same claim, condition moved to the front:

  "In a system-paced presentation, route words away from the visual channel when a graphic is
   present: pictures load the visual/pictorial channel and spoken words the auditory/verbal
   channel, but printed and onscreen text enters through the eyes first and competes with the
   graphic for the same limited channel. Prefer narration over concurrent onscreen text."

Confirmed: `compile_invariants ... | grep P157` and `adapter:158` now both open "In a system-paced
presentation". Also gave the one-line P157 restatement in
`references/instructional-design-principles-index.md` the same bound.

Digest fallout handled: the three authored docs citing P157 (`multimedia-and-elearning-design` and
both references) went STALE on the statement change and were re-stamped with
`detect_stale --stamp`. Their bodies already stated "system-paced", so grounding did not move —
only the upstream digest. `detect_stale` is clean (all OK).

## MUST-FIX 2 — P107/P134 cited to ground ownership/authority claims they do not state

P107 grounds making the teaching theory explicit and adapting to local learners/constraints; P134
grounds systematic action-research cycles. Neither states who *owns* the course, the subject
matter, the grades, or the decision to run it. All four sites fixed in `profile.yaml`:

1. `source_of_truth_policy.precedence` — dropped `P107`; `P193` now attaches only to the
   subject-matter-referral clause it supports. Ownership clause stands unmarked as factory policy.
2. `handoff_rules[0]` — dropped `P107, P134`; `P021` retained on the criterion-based
   outcome-judgement clause.
3. `source_of_truth_policy.canonical_owner` — split, so `(P107, P134)` attaches only to the
   make-the-theory-explicit / adapt-through-systematic-evidence-grounded-cycles clause; final
   authority over the course, its materials, and what is taught is now stated separately and
   uncited.
4. `forbidden_behaviours[4]` — dropped the spurious `P107`; `P021` + `P172` already ground it fully.

Force of the boundary is unchanged — the advisor still never builds, teaches, grades, or certifies.
Only the false grounding was removed, so the hedge is stated as policy instead of as
principle-derived (`.claude/rules/rights-and-quotation-policy.md`, "No orphan field values").

